    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0139" n="31" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg31"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">April 28,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 258.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received Mr. Markell’s No. 408 of
                    the 13th ultimo, reporting that he has been advised by the Government of Brazil
                    that the export duties on skins improperly collected by the State of Bahia will
                    be returned to the exporters on presentation of their claims to the treasury of
                    the State, and that similar action will be recommended by the governor of
                    Pernambuco to the State legislature.</p>
                <pb facs="0140" n="32" xml:id="pg32"/>
                <p>You will express to the Brazilian Government our satisfaction at the action taken
                    by the State of Bahia, and our hope that that of the State of Pernambuco will be
                    equally satisfactory.</p>
                <p>The consuls at Bahia and Pernambuco will be advised.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alyey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
